  every candidate here either opens a row or names the one already open

A run may draft for a listed surface. It may not do so without
naming the candidate already open on it, because that is the
difference between superseding a draft and not knowing it exists.
And a candidate for a surface with no row at all opens one, because
an unregistered draft is a line nobody will ever come back to.

